From 90f977170d19f7cf1e11337181e74d08503a49d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xavi Ivars <xavi.ivars@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 02:04:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Add the I18n translation primitive
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

qs.Commons.I18n and its Qt-free model, plus the Bash counterpart for
bin/ scripts. No call sites change and no catalogs ship: with nothing
registered every lookup returns its source string.

Catalogs are contributed by owners — a language pack is one — and merged
by precedence. A startup cache of the merged result is read synchronously
so the first frame is already translated rather than repainting once the
packs finish registering.

That cache is a stand-in, not a second copy: it registers as an ordinary
owner at the lowest precedence, and is dropped as soon as a live owner
registers. Otherwise disabling a pack leaves the cache still holding an
identical copy of the strings it just removed, and the interface stays
translated until the next restart. For the same reason the snapshot
written to disk excludes it, and it will not reload over live data —
writing the cache re-triggers the FileView that loads it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 default/bash/i18n          | 130 +++++++++++
 shell/Commons/I18n.qml     | 182 +++++++++++++++
 shell/Commons/I18nModel.js | 445 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 shell/Commons/qmldir       |   1 +
 4 files changed, 758 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 default/bash/i18n
